Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:04:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Home: Continue only for a self-check really left
 part-way; 44 px tonight links (U18 review)

- continueHere: a self-check whose saved answers are the ones its last
  result was taken from is finished, however recently they were saved.
  Seeing the results again, or "Change my answers" and changing nothing,
  saved the answers after the result without a new run, so Home kept
  offering "Continue" for a finished check. Compare the answers'
  fingerprint (SelfCheckHistory's answersKey, with the Life Audit's
  set-aside areas) as well as the dates. Tested, and checked in Chromium
  through the Emotional Health self-check.
- The tonight and Continue links measured 40 px tall; their padding now
  gives 46 px, with a little more room between the two rows.
- A stale comment ("Not a fourth door") now that Home has four doors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
